builds a fetch URL whose userinfo part holds the bot user and `gerrit_bot_token` and passes it as a positional argument to `git fetch -q --depth 2`. The secret is therefore in the git process's command line for the length of the fetch. On 2026-11-22 at 19:32 PST a read-only `ps` sample on the prod host (taken for ultrashort-emaciated-krill) showed the full URL, password included, in the review-bot's git child. Anyone who can list processes on the host or in the container (`ps`, `/proc/<pid>/cmdline`, SSM command output, monitoring agents) can read it. The token is the review-bot account's dual-scope Gerrit credential (REST and git).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No review-bot git invocation carries a credential in its argv; the fetch authenticates through a channel that is not in the command line (credential helper, or a header passed through the environment).\n- [ ] A test fails if `clone_change_ref` puts the bot token in the git argv.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The review-bot Gerrit token is rotated after the fix deploys, since it has appeared in process listings.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7279-b619-cb42-40b8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Review-bot passes its Gerrit HTTP password in git's argv, visible in any process listing","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c04275d7-cc90-4925-a646-e31cd9e32f8b","cdb8441c-ff96-44ae-8bfc-45075ce395ff"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795406687786562002,"uuid":"1f0d2f7a-c37f-4092-bbe3-a8b883d90885"}